{"kind": "chat_performance", "workload": "explanation", "repeat": 1, "prompt": "Explain how hash tables handle collisions, resizing, and adversarial input. Compare separate chaining with open addressing and give practical examples.", "input_ids": [248045, 846, 198, 814, 20139, 1204, 5010, 12269, 3579, 45776, 11, 83264, 11, 321, 27483, 41306, 1879, 13, 23024, 8387, 71159, 440, 1724, 26153, 321, 2873, 14542, 9989, 13, 248046, 198, 248045, 74455, 198, 248068, 271, 248069, 271], "prompt_tokens": 38, "output_tokens": 256, "answer": "Hash tables are fundamental data structures that provide average-case $O(1)$ time complexity for insertions, deletions, and lookups. However, achieving this performance requires careful handling of three critical challenges: **collisions**, **resizing**, and **adversarial inputs**.\n\nBelow is a detailed explanation of these mechanisms, followed by a comparison of collision resolution strategies and practical examples.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Handling Collisions\n\nA collision occurs when two distinct keys hash to the same index in the underlying array. Since the hash function maps a large key space to a smaller array index space, collisions are inevitable (Pigeonhole Principle).\n\n#### A. Separate Chaining\nIn separate chaining, each bucket in the hash table array points to a linked list (or another dynamic structure) of entries that hash to that index.\n\n- **Mechanism**: When a collision occurs, the new entry is appended to the list at that bucket.\n- **Pros**:\n  - Simple to implement.\n  - The table never becomes \"full\" in the sense that insertion is always possible (memory permitting).\n  - Deletion is straightforward.\n- **Cons**:\n  - Poor cache locality (pointer chasing).\n  - Performance degrades to", "input_sha256": "2d4cd832e51e7b84accb51b33cdbe69630c5b76dc17c0986f9fdaf9d6248b23b", "output_sha256": "b0ee38da55f1211cb8436e346fe252166bc665c673e85a0870cbca3b6ca9d215", "ttft_seconds": 1.04950762540102, "elapsed_seconds": 12.672475293278694, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 38, "prompt_ms": 1004.0, "prompt_per_token_ms": 26.421, "prompt_per_second": 37.8, "predicted_n": 256, "predicted_ms": 11666.4, "predicted_per_token_ms": 45.572, "predicted_per_second": 21.9, "draft_n": 0, "draft_n_accepted": 0}, "engine": {"generated": 256, "prompt_tokens": 38, "prompt_ms": 1004.0, "decode_ms": 11666.4, "finish": "length", "drafts_accepted": 0, "drafts_offered": 0, "reused": 0, "hits": 121770, "lookups": 122880, "ram_blobs": 1110, "file_blobs": 0, "file_mb": 0.0, "prompt_read": 38, "offloaded": 0, "chunk": 0, "experts_streamed": 0}, "gpus": 2, "workers": 8, "profile": false, "aux_cpus": "off", "mode": "layer", "shared_stream": "default"}
{"kind": "chat_performance", "workload": "chinese", "repeat": 1, "prompt": "请详细说明分布式任务队列如何处理任务重试、幂等、超时和工作节点故障，并给出一个具体例子。", "input_ids": [248045, 846, 198, 96220, 128110, 112149, 97995, 113165, 126829, 97995, 145748, 5205, 103557, 96024, 5205, 132980, 110671, 101971, 101775, 3709, 96172, 110334, 96125, 97990, 102177, 1710, 248046, 198, 248045, 74455, 198, 248068, 271, 248069, 271], "prompt_tokens": 35, "output_tokens": 256, "answer": "# 分布式任务队列：重试、幂等、超时与故障处理详解\n\n## 一、整体架构概览\n\n```\n┌─────────────┐     ┌──────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────┐\n│  Producer   │────▶│  Message Broker  │────▶│  Worker Pool    │\n│ (任务生产者) │     │  (RabbitMQ/Redis │     │ (工作节点集群)   │\n└─────────────┘     │   /Kafka等)      │     └────────┬────────┘\n                    └──────────────────┘              │\n                                                      ▼\n                                              ┌───────────────┐\n                                              │  Result Store │\n                                              │  (DB/Redis)   │\n                                              └───────────────┘\n```\n\n核心挑战：**分布式环境下，网络分区、节点崩溃、消息重复投递、处理超时**等问题不可避免。下面逐一深入分析。\n\n---\n\n## 二、四大核心问题详解\n\n### 1. 任务重试（Retry）\n\n#### 为什么需要重试？\n- 瞬时故障：网络抖动、数据库连接池耗尽、第三方API限流\n", "input_sha256": "7d6c91f3356f57478fac3800d43abad2970bf52f3985e8e9b3733fc8606b5ada", "output_sha256": "81254d1ab7a78687791031f7b3bdb73cf73aabcaf31025e3820a4e8184bee2a8", "ttft_seconds": 0.9559068530797958, "elapsed_seconds": 12.780864298343658, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 35, "prompt_ms": 910.2, "prompt_per_token_ms": 26.006, "prompt_per_second": 38.5, "predicted_n": 256, "predicted_ms": 11868.9, "predicted_per_token_ms": 46.363, "predicted_per_second": 21.6, "draft_n": 0, "draft_n_accepted": 0}, "engine": {"generated": 256, "prompt_tokens": 35, "prompt_ms": 910.2, "decode_ms": 11868.9, "finish": "length", "drafts_accepted": 0, "drafts_offered": 0, "reused": 0, "hits": 119373, "lookups": 122880, "ram_blobs"